# Rust
/target/
/target2/
Cargo.lock

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# Claude Code — local state stays ignored, but project slash COMMANDS are
# versioned (they encode project doctrine, e.g. /triage-wave's >30%-FP gate).
# NOTE: `.claude/*` (not `.claude/`) so the negation below can re-include the
# commands dir — git never descends into a fully-ignored directory.
.claude/*
!.claude/commands/
tmpclaude-*

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Scratch artifacts (root-level analysis output)
/out*.sarif
/perf_stderr.txt
# Measurement/run logs (perf traces, detached 8020 runs) and demo/report output —
# large, machine-local, regenerable; never part of the repo's evidence surface
# (committed evidence lives in docs/ and .superpowers/sdd/ reports).
/logs/
/demo-out/
# Local tooling state (panel-review scratch, Serena project cache)
/.panel/
/.serena/

# MCP server config — LOCAL ONLY. The working copy carries per-developer service
# endpoints AND credentials in its `env` blocks (bc / bc-dev container logins), so
# it must never be committed as-is. It is deliberately NOT shared: sharing it with
# the team means first moving every secret out of `env` into environment variables
# and committing only the indirection.
/.mcp.json

# 1B.3b Task 1: local-only de-anonymization map (AnonId -> plaintext) for the
# committed anonymized CDO goldens under tests/goldens/semantic-edges/. NEVER
# committed — see src/program/resolve/anon.rs's module docs.
tests/goldens/semantic-edges/cdo-deanon-map.json
.agent-review/

# agentflow (the autonomous issue orchestrator) — local state is ignored; the two
# per-issue evidence files are versioned. Pattern shape matters: `.agent/*` plus
# re-includes, because git never descends into a fully-ignored directory.
.agent/*
!.agent/issue-*/
.agent/issue-*/*
!.agent/issue-*/ledger.md
!.agent/issue-*/findings.json

# agentflow's test suite (scripts/agentflow/tests/) — nothing else in the repo
# ignores these.
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
